  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Rights-Based Solutions for Vulnerable Migrants Through a Migrant Resource and Response Mechanism (MRRM) In East Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Libya has traditionally been an origin, transit and destination country for migrants seeking better economic opportunities, escaping oppressive conditions in their home countries, or hoping to use the territory as a launch pad to Europe. Migration dynamics in Libya remain complex and challenging, with many migrants across the country confronting significant protection risks related to socio-economic vulnerabilities as well as their status. Vulnerable migrants in need of immediate assistance include victims of trafficking, survivors of gender-based violence and unaccompanied and separated children. Through an integrated approach, IOM designed the Migrant Resource and Response Mechanism (MRRM) which brings together in one mechanism a wide range of services and needs-based assistance to migrants  in urban areas, as well as carrying out vulnerability screening for referral to appropriate services including protection services. While the MRRM is currently operating in Tripoli, Bani Waleed, Qatroun, Sabha, Zwara and Ghat there is no such system for Ejdabya region, East of Libya, where there are acute pockets of humanitarian needs. This project aims to launch MRRM in Ejdabya. Through the MRRM base and mobile teams in Ejdabya, migrants living in urban areas will benefit from health, mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS), direct assistance as well as referrals to specialised protection services and other public or non-governmental service providers. With this project IOM will reach at last 4,000 beneficiaries with one or more services.</narrative>
  </description>
